    rdf:value """the High Altar of the Duomo. Also a drink of warm milk I extracted from a cow by the wayside. 
4. The Giovanni Pisanos and Simone Martinis at Pisa, and the row down the river in a fisherman’s barge, with a sight of the camels feeding along the bank. 
Today at lunch Bernhard suddenly broke out in praise of the Degas on the mantelpiece, “the greatest of all works of art.” “Why?” … A good deal of hesitation and feeling round, and at last the right reason hit on the head, because it  conveys life directly . He has deserted the theory that art is to “ uplift ”, or “ broaden ” life, or any """^^xsd:string ;
